Camera name: Starling 2 Max (VOXL 2 / QRB5165), C29 camera config (stereo + ToF)
Rig name: netted mocap volume, indoor, person-following flight test
Vehicle: ModalAI Starling 2 Max, PX4 running on the VOXL 2 sensors DSP
Firmware: PX4 (voxl-px4), autopilot component 1

INDOOR PROFILE -- committed 15-week internship scope (8 Sep - 20 Dec 2026).

Flight context this file is tuned for:
  - Flown inside a netted OptiTrack/mocap volume, walls and net a few metres
    from the takeoff point in every direction.
  - A person (the "operator") stands or walks inside or at the edge of the
    same volume while the vehicle follows them.
  - Autonomous following runs the vehicle in PX4 Offboard mode, driven by
    voxl-mapper trajectories relayed through voxl-vision-hub
    (offboard_mode="trajectory", see config/voxl-vision-hub.conf).
  - A safety pilot holds a live RC link at all times and can take manual
    Position-mode control instantly (see docs/SAFETY.md for the full
    protocol and roles).

Load with: QGroundControl > Vehicle Setup > Parameters > Tools > Load from
file. Or on the VOXL shell: `param load /path/to/this/file` after copying
it to the vehicle (adjust extension/tooling to your PX4 param loader).

File format (matches the schema this repo uses for exported params):
  index    0-based line index in this file, informational only
  vehicle_id     MAVLink system id the parameter applies to (1 = this vehicle)
  component_id   MAVLink component id (1 = autopilot)
  param_name     PX4 parameter name
  value          parameter value as written to the FMU
  type           MAVLink param type: 6 = INT32 (enums/bitmasks/counts),
                 9 = FLOAT32 (continuous/physical quantities)

RESEARCH-VERIFIED FACTS THIS FILE IS BUILT AROUND (see docs/SAFETY.md for the
full citations and the failsafe matrix that follows from them):
  (1) PX4 Collision Prevention (CP_*) only functions in Position mode with
      MPC_POS_MODE set to an acceleration-based mode. It is NOT active in
      Offboard mode. It is a piloted-testing safety net, never the
      autonomous avoidance layer -- that job belongs to voxl-mapper/VOA.
  (2) PX4's geofence is REACTIVE: it fires only after the boundary has
      already been crossed. PX4's own docs say a strict boundary needs
      GF_ACTION=Hold plus a safety margin built into the fence size, since
      the vehicle will have already breached the fence line by the time the
      action triggers.
  (3) When multiple failsafes trigger at once, PX4 executes the MOST SEVERE
      action. Severity order (least to most): None, Warning, Hold, Return,
      Land, Disarm, Flight termination.
  (4) Collision Prevention restricts velocity to ZERO in any direction with
      no sensor data unless CP_GO_NO_DATA=1. There is a hard watchdog: more
      than 0.5 s with no range data blocks all further movement in that
      direction, and 5 s with no data forces a HOLD.

