# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Per-parameter rationale (why this value, for THIS indoor/netted profile)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# GF_MAX_HOR_DIST = 8.0 m (float)
#   Cylindrical geofence radius from the arming point. Sized to sit INSIDE
#   the netting with margin: measure your actual mocap volume's usable
#   radius and set this to (usable radius - 1.5 m) at minimum, because
#   fact (2) means the vehicle will already be past this line before the
#   fence action fires -- the margin is what keeps it off the net. 8 m
#   assumes a ~10-11 m diameter tracked volume; MEASURE YOUR ROOM and
#   adjust down if your net is closer than that.
#
# GF_MAX_VER_DIST = 3.0 m (float)
#   Vertical geofence half-extent. Assumes a typical ceiling-mounted mocap
#   rig with usable ceiling height around 4-4.5 m; leaves margin above the
#   follow altitude (FollowParams.height_m = 2.0 m in follow_core) for
#   overshoot before the reactive fence engages. MEASURE YOUR CEILING
#   HEIGHT and the mocap camera mounting height and adjust so this stays
#   at least 1 m below both.
#
# GF_ACTION = 2 (Hold) [int32]
#   Per fact (2): PX4's own guidance for a strict/tight boundary is Hold,
#   not Return, because Return still commands lateral flight (back toward
#   home) after an already-reactive trigger, covering more ground next to
#   a person and the net. Hold simply stops the vehicle where it is and
#   waits for the safety pilot.
#
# COM_OF_LOSS_T = 0.5 s (float)
#   Offboard-loss timeout: how long the FMU waits without a fresh Offboard
#   setpoint before declaring offboard control lost. Kept short indoors --
#   near a person, a stalled companion computer / voxl-mapper trajectory
#   feed should hand control back to the pilot fast, not coast for seconds
#   on the last setpoint.
#
# COM_OBL_RC_ACT = 0 (Position) [int32]
#   Action taken on offboard loss WHEN RC is present (this is the indoor
#   case -- the safety pilot always holds a live RC link, see SAFETY.md).
#   Falls back to Position mode rather than Land/RTL so the pilot regains
#   normal manual control immediately and can fly the vehicle away from
#   the person/net by hand. NOTE: Position mode is also the only mode in
#   which Collision Prevention (CP_*) is active per fact (1), so this
#   fallback is also what re-arms the CP safety net.
#
# COM_RC_LOSS_T = 0.5 s (float)
#   RC-signal-loss timeout. PX4 default; short on purpose so a genuine RC
#   dropout indoors (short range, lots of multipath off the net/mocap
#   rig) is declared quickly rather than flying on into the volume.
#
# NAV_RCL_ACT = 3 (Land) [int32]
#   Action on RC loss. Land, not Return, because indoors "Return" means
#   flying laterally back across the netted volume -- possibly toward
#   the operator -- with no RC override available. Landing in place is
#   the lower-energy, more predictable outcome in a confined space.
#
# COM_RCL_EXCEPT = 0 (no exceptions) [int32]
#   Bitmask of conditions that are allowed to suppress the RC-loss
#   failsafe (e.g. during a mission). Left at 0 indoors: there is no
#   mission phase where continuing to fly without RC is acceptable next
#   to a person, so no exception bits are set.
#
# CP_DIST = 1.0 m (float)
#   Collision Prevention keep-out distance. Only meaningful in Position
#   mode per fact (1) -- this is the piloted-testing safety net, not the
#   autonomous avoidance layer. Set tighter than the 1.25 m PX4 default
#   because the room is small; if CP_DIST were left larger than half the
#   room, CP could refuse motion almost everywhere. MEASURE your room and
#   keep CP_DIST comfortably smaller than the tightest wall clearance you
#   need to fly through.
#
# CP_DELAY = 0.4 s (float)
#   PX4 default system-latency compensation for Collision Prevention
#   (sensor + processing delay). Not changed for this profile; there is
#   no indoor-specific reason to move it and it has not been re-measured
#   against the VOXL 2's actual pipeline latency.
#
# CP_GUIDE_ANG = 30 deg (float)
#   PX4 default guidance angle (how far CP will steer around an obstacle
#   edge instead of just stopping). Left at default; only relevant in
#   Position mode per fact (1), and 30 deg is a reasonable compromise in
#   a small room where there usually isn't space to route far around.
#
# CP_GO_NO_DATA = 0 (disabled) [int32]
#   Per fact (4): with this at 0 (PX4 default), CP commands ZERO velocity
#   in any direction lacking sensor data, with a hard watchdog (0.5 s no
#   data blocks movement that way, 5 s forces HOLD). Left at 0 (the
#   conservative choice) deliberately: with a person in the same small
#   volume, "no sensor data = don't move that way" is the correct default,
#   even though it means CP will refuse motion into sensor blind spots.
#
# MPC_POS_MODE = 4 (Smooth Position Control, acceleration-based) [int32]
#   Per fact (1), Collision Prevention ONLY functions when MPC_POS_MODE is
#   an acceleration-based mode -- this is the parameter that makes the CP_*
#   safety net (above) actually active during piloted Position-mode
#   testing. Mode 4 (jerk-limited smooth position control) is used instead
#   of the plain acceleration-based mode 3 for gentler stick response
#   next to a person.
#
# MPC_XY_VEL_MAX = 1.0 m/s (float)
#   Horizontal speed cap. Conservative on purpose: this is an order of
#   magnitude below the outdoor cap (config/px4_starling_outdoor.params)
#   because the vehicle operates within a few metres of a person inside a
#   netted volume. Cross-check against the follow_core FollowParams
#   near-target speed cap (speed_cap_near_m_s = 0.6 m/s) so the autonomy
#   layer's commanded speed is already inside what the FMU will accept.
#
# MPC_Z_VEL_MAX_UP = 1.0 m/s (float)
#   Vertical ascent speed cap. Matched to the horizontal cap; no reason
#   for climb to be faster than horizontal travel in this small volume.
#
# MPC_Z_VEL_MAX_DN = 0.7 m/s (float)
#   Vertical descent speed cap, kept slower than ascent (PX4 convention)
#   since an uncommanded fast descent is the worse failure mode with a
#   person standing underneath.
#
# MPC_TILTMAX_AIR = 20 deg (float)
#   Max tilt angle in flight, well below the PX4 default (~45 deg).
#   Directly bounds both max achievable acceleration and how "sharp" any
#   avoidance or follow maneuver can look right next to a person -- a
#   deliberate trade of agility for predictability indoors.
#
# COM_OBS_AVOID = 1 (enabled) [int32]
#   Enables the onboard obstacle-avoidance data path (the OBSTACLE_DISTANCE
#   / VOA plumbing from voxl-vision-hub) so PX4 accepts and displays it.
#   NOTE: enabling this does not itself make avoidance "active" in
#   Offboard mode the way Collision Prevention is in Position mode -- in
#   Offboard, voxl-mapper is the component that must route around the ESDF
#   obstacle map (config/voxl-mapper.conf) BEFORE it ever hands PX4 a
#   trajectory. Treat this flag as "let the data through," not "avoidance
#   is guaranteed."
